  "purpose": "Machine-readable crate dependency topology. Single source of truth for the DAG, the layer assignment, and crate justification. Replaces the prose taxonomy in AGENTS.md and the tables in infra/CANONICAL_CRATE_MAP.md, which can drift from the build graph and from each other and are not executable. A vertical slice names crates; this file gives the topological order to extract them in.",
  "authority_order": [
    "observed runtime state",
    "contracts/foundation.json",
    "infra/runtime-authority.json",
    "infra/directory-tree.json",
    "this file",
    "infra/registry.json",
    "workspace Cargo.toml",
    "canonical crates"
  ],
  "layer_rule": "A crate may depend only on a strictly lower layer. L0 is pure: no I/O, no adapter. cross_cutting is unlayered and may be depended on from any layer. Equal-layer edges are legal and are the normal case inside L2; they are listed explicitly so a new one is a deliberate act.",
  "justification_rule": "Every member must be a binary, have at least one dependent, or appear in pending_disposition with a written reason. A crate that is none of these is a node with in-degree zero: it cannot take part in a runtime loop, and every layer that names it is describing a boundary nothing crosses. pending_disposition may only shrink.",
